#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# integers

#% text
# `integers` is the domain of the integers ..., -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, ..., for facts `element(x, integers)` in `assuming` and `refine`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `element(x, integers)` with a number `x` is decided at once: `true` or `false`. With a symbol it is a fact that `assuming` adds to the assumptions.

#% item
# Functions that use assumptions (`simplify`, `refine`, `power_expand` and the sign tests) take the domain into account.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
element(3, integers)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(-7, integers)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
element(1/2, integers)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
element(pi, integers)
#% output
#= false

#% text
# A symbol in the domain:

#% cell
assuming(element(n, integers), refine(sin(n*pi)))
#% output
#= 0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
assuming(element(n, integers), refine(cos(2*pi*n)))
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A symbol alone is not decided:

#% cell
element(x, integers)
#% output
#= element(x, integers)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `element`, `assuming`, `refine`, `rationals`, `reals`
